# Post-fix drill run log (2026-11-11 ~20:40 CET, after #118 deploy)

Harness: coco master @ 2d6aa583 (coco-sync clone, packages/core +
sqlite-bun), logging proxy 127.0.0.1:8907 -> testnut.cashu.exchange.
phase1: INJECT_FROM_SWAP=2 (every reclaim attempt 502'd, not forwarded).
phase2: INJECT_OFF=1 (fresh proxy process), fresh wallet process, same
sqlite db + persisted random seed. Artifacts: wire-postfix.jsonl,
drill-postfix.ts, drill-proxy-postfix.ts (this dir).

Driver deltas vs the banked pre-fix drill (the pre-fix pair never got
past the mint block, so its back half was unvalidated): port 8899->8907
(8899 was occupied by an unrelated lane's local mint), seed must be
64 bytes (SeedService enforces), random-once-then-persisted seed
(fixed seed + fresh db re-derives the same secrets -> "spent proof"
400s from earlier runs), mint terminal state is 'finalized' (not
'completed') and needs a wait loop (execute() returns pending; the
claim happens via watcher/re-execute), public API is
reclaim()/cancel() (no sendOps.rollback), cancel only works pre-
execute, and the rollback path retries the reclaim internally (a
single-shot injection lets the retry through -> inject ALL swaps >= 2
for phase1).

## phase1 (crash-mid-rollback)

  [phase1] mint op terminal state: finalized
  [phase1] balance after mint: {"spendable":"21","reserved":"0","total":"21","unit":"sat"}
  [phase1] send prepared / send state after execute: pending
  [coco:warn] Could not settle a failed Send reclaim; leaving it for recovery
  [phase1] reclaim rejected as expected: bad response
  [phase1] persisted send state: rolling_back
  [coco:warn] Ignoring Mint Quote Observation with conflicting accounting
              at unchanged Remote Quote Update Time   <-- cf residue, see below

  swaps: #1 200 (send: in 16 -> out 1+2+4+8=15, 1 sat fee)
         #2 INJECTED (reclaim: in 8+2 -> out 1+8=9)
         #3 INJECTED (retry, byte-identical to #2)

## phase2 (fresh process, injection off)

  [phase2] state before recovery: rolled_back   <-- settled by STARTUP
                                               auto-recovery (Manager boots
                                               with ops.send.recovery.run());
                                               no explicit command needed
  [phase2] balance after recovery: {"spendable":"19",...,"total":"19"}

  swap #4 200: replayed reclaim, reqBody byte-identical to the
  interrupted #2/#3 (inputs [8,2] -> outputs [1,8]).

  Economics: 21 -> 19 = exactly 2 x 1-sat swap fees (send + reclaim).
  No loss. FIRST LIVE coco-mints-from-testnut proof is in this same
  wire log (POST /v1/mint/bolt11 200, signatures 16+4+1, quote check
  responses now carry amount_paid/amount_issued/updated_at).

## The remaining cf residue this run exposed (live-on-main, NOT vintage)

1. Certifier leg "NUT-04 #377-epoch GET accounting after full mint"
   stays RED post-deploy: GET /v1/mint/quote/bolt11/{id} serves
   amount_issued=0, updated_at unmoved, state=PAID after a successful
   full mint (the stored write the batch-check path sees never reaches
   the GET read path). Pre-registered in get-path-stale-accounting.txt
   as "expected deploy-vintage" — that prediction was WRONG; verdict:
   live-on-main. Filed as its own issue.
2. updated_at is not bumped when issuance accounting changes, even on
   the (correct) batch-check path: coco's NUT-04 anti-stale guard
   ("MUST NOT replace quote data with a response whose updated_at is
   lower / conflicting accounting at unchanged update time") discards
   the post-mint observation every time. Benign for this flow (the op
   finalizes from the mint response itself) but it makes every
   spec-compliant wallet blind to cf issuance accounting.
